From dd460af0212eb747816c609bb295bacea47c0dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:36:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: method lookup prefers stable methods over
 unstable library ones

shellexpand 3.1.1 (mcfly 0.9.4) funcs.rs:394, `var_name: &str` with the
crate's in-scope `WstrExt::as_str(&self) -> Option<&str>`:

    let var_name = match var_name.as_str() {
        Some(var_name) => var_name,
        None => return Ok(None),
    };

    funcs.rs:398:19 error:0: Type mismatch between str and Option<_>

core 1.90 has `#[unstable(feature = "str_as_str")] pub fn as_str(&self)
-> &str` on `str`. mrustc kept no stability information and inherent
methods win, so core's method was picked. rustc (method/probe.rs
`pick_core`) first probes every autoderef level without the unstable
methods of features the crate hasn't enabled, and takes one of those
only when nothing else applies. Same class: num-integer's
`a.div_floor(&b)` (core's unstable `i32::div_floor(self, Self)`),
itertools' `i.intersperse(x)` through an `I: Iterator` bound (core's
unstable `Iterator::intersperse` was the bound's method), and the path
forms `str::as_str(s)` / `i32::div_floor(&a, &b)` in Resolve UFCS.

- `HIR::Function::Markings::unstable_feature`: the item's
  `#[unstable(feature = "..")]`, or that of an `#[unstable]` inherent
  impl block for a method without its own stability attribute. It is
  serialised: rlibs written by an older mrustc can't be loaded.
- `HIR::Crate::m_enabled_features` (not serialised): `#![feature(..)]`
  plus the crate's own unstable features (rustc never stability-checks
  local items).
- autoderef_find_method runs a probe that skips unstable methods
  (inherent, bound, trait object, in-scope trait), then a second one
  with them if the first found nothing but skipped one.
- resolve_ufcs: an unstable inherent item is skipped, and retried
  before "Failed to find impl".

Not modelled: `implied_by`, inheritance from an unstable trait to its
methods, `-Z force-unstable-if-unmarked`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
